  "help.title": "Colvio Help",
  "help.subtitle": "Quick guide for D365 consultants",
  "help.getting_started_title": "Getting Started",
  "help.getting_started_body": "1. Open Colvio on a Dynamics 365 page\n2. Select an entity in the sidebar\n3. Choose fields and filters\n4. Execute with Ctrl+Enter\n5. Export results as CSV, XLSX, or JSON",
  "help.explorer_title": "Data Explorer",
  "help.explorer_body": "Query D365 data using the visual Builder, raw OData, FetchXML, or SQL. Add filters, expand lookups, and paginate results. Ctrl+Enter to execute.\nQuery tabs: open several queries at once (+ New), like browser tabs. Each tab is fully independent — its own table, query mode, filters and results — so you run them one at a time and switch between tabs to compare. Double-click a tab to rename it, ✕ to close.\nLIMIT now defaults to All (everything, auto-paginated) — lower it when you just want a quick preview.\nREL — relation filters (Advanced-Find style): filter the ROOT rows by related records. On a parent (N:1): a condition on the parent's fields (\"accounts whose primary contact's email contains @gmail\"). On children (1:N): \"has at least one\" / \"has none\" matching children (\"accounts with no open opportunity\") — with optional conditions on the child. Unlike EXPAND (which only changes what's displayed), REL changes which rows come back. Combined with your WHERE via AND; the generated OData is visible in the query preview. Note: parent paths go one level deep (Dataverse limit) — deeper chains need FetchXML link-entities.",
  "help.show_title": "Show All Data",
  "help.show_body": "Paste a D365 record URL or enter an entity name and GUID to inspect all fields and values of a single record. Fields render in a responsive multi-column grid that fills the screen, so even 400+ field records stay readable. Filter columns, toggle empty/custom-only, and copy a single field or the full JSON.\nWritable fields show a ✎ pencil: edit the value inline (text, numbers, yes/no, dates, option sets) and save it straight through the API — even when the form marks the field read-only. Field-level security and write privileges still apply, and production asks for confirmation first.",
  "help.metadata_title": "Metadata Browser",
  "help.metadata_body": "Browse entity fields, types, and OptionSet values. Export all OptionSets for an entity as CSV in one click.",
  "help.loader_title": "Data Loader",
  "help.loader_body": "Import CSV, TSV or Excel (XLSX) files into D365 through a 5-step wizard: Source → Mapping → Lookups → Preview → Run. Drag-drop a file or paste from a spreadsheet (delimiter auto-detected: comma, tab or semicolon — quoted cells, embedded commas and line breaks are handled). Columns auto-map to D365 fields; lookup-type columns are detected and routed to the Parent Lookups step. Mapping templates let you save and reload a full configuration (mappings, lookups, key, mode) per entity. The live log shows every row with its CSV values, the exact request sent, and Success/Failed status with the Dataverse error message.\nEmpty cell vs NULL: an empty cell always leaves the field untouched (a partial file can't wipe data). To actually CLEAR a field — including a lookup — put the literal word NULL in the cell (any case). For COMPLETE files where empty really means 'must be empty', the per-run option 'Empty cells CLEAR fields' inverts the contract: every empty cell in a mapped column sends an explicit null (a pre-flight warning counts exactly how many cells will clear; in delta mode, clears matching an already-empty org value are skipped).",
  "help.loader_modes_title": "Loader — the 4 import modes",
  "help.loader_modes_body": "CREATE — every row becomes a new record (POST).\nUPSERT — rows are matched on the key you pick: existing records are updated, missing ones are created. Choose an alternate key (🔑 shown at the top of the key dropdown) and Colvio binds directly via entityset(key='value') with no GUID resolution query.\nUPDATE (existing only) — strictly update: every PATCH carries the native If-Match: * header, so Dataverse returns 404 instead of creating when the record doesn't exist. A row with an empty key fails too — nothing is ever created. Optional \"verify each record exists first\" pre-check for orgs that don't honor If-Match on alternate keys.\nDELETE — removes records matched on the key (GUID or alternate key). Requires typing a confirmation before the run starts.\nThe key never needs to be in your data twice: it addresses the record in the URL, the other columns form the body.",
  "help.transforms_title": "Loader — column transforms",
  "help.transforms_body": "Each mapped column can have a transform:\n• picklist / statecode — accepts the numeric value OR the option label: \"Chaud\", \"3 - Hot\"… Colvio pre-loads the field's OptionSet and converts labels to values; labels that match nothing are listed in the result panel instead of being silently dropped.\n• date ISO — accepts yyyy-mm-dd (kept as-is, no timezone shift), dd/mm/yyyy (EU) and mm/dd/yyyy (US auto-detected when the month is >12), with optional time (24h or AM/PM) converted to a proper ISO timestamp.\n• int / float — locale-aware: \"1 000\", \"1,5\" and \"1.234,56\" parse correctly.\n• strip HTML → plain text — removes the markup and keeps the visible text (entities decoded, <br>/<p> become line breaks, lists become \"- \" bullets). Use it when the source is rich text (HTML) but the target column is plain text; the max-length pre-flight measures the stripped text, not the raw HTML.\n• boolean, yes/no (EN+FR), UPPER/lower.\nValues are trimmed automatically — stray spaces never end up in keys or fields.",
  "recyclebin.title": "Recycle Bin",
  "recyclebin.subtitle": "View and restore records deleted from Dataverse — a true server-side restore, not a copy.",
